{
 "version": 1,
 "about": "The installer's decisions on observed facts, read by apps/codex/internal/install's tests and tests/install-verify-test.sh. systems: /etc/os-release text and the CPU architecture, whether automatic preparation supports them and the system named in refusals. universe: the output of `apt-get indextargets --no-release-info --format '$(RELEASE) $(COMPONENT) $(IDENTIFIER)'` and the release codename, whether universe's packages are enabled. bootstrap: the install script's facts (supported system, universe enabled, a verification bypass set, commands on PATH, packages dpkg reports installed, read on the supported system alone) and the packages it offers before release verification; cosign is not needed under a bypass. init: cyfr init's facts (internal/install.Facts) and its decision: the outcome, the root actions in order, the refusal's cause and whether init continues in a process carrying the docker group.",
